Demi Lovato Brings Out Joe Jonas for Surprise &#8216;Camp Rock&#8217; Duet at Tour Opening: &#8216;Did You Miss&nbsp;Us?&#8217;

That goes especially for the many concertgoers with deep nostalgic attachment to the pop star&#8217;s older hits, many of which she played alongside tracks from 2025 album It&#8217;s Not That Deep on Monday (April 13) at the Kia Center. The trek supports the LP &#8212; which reached No. 9 on the Billboard 200 &#8212; and its setlist features several of the new songs, including lead single &#8220;Fast.&#8221; But Lovato also performed a number of older Billboard Hot 100 hits, from &#8220;Heart Attack&#8221; to &#8220;Cool for the Summer,&#8221; &#8220;Confident&#8221; and &#8220;Tell Me You Love Me.&#8221;

Plus, the opening show was complete with a very special guest: Joe Jonas, who helped Lovato perform two Disney Channel-era duets on stage, including one iconic Camp Rock duet. In the crowd, the night&#8217;s headliner&#8217;s Princess Protection Program costar and longtime friend Selena Gomez looked on proudly, later writing on Instagram Stories, “I am in tears. @ddlovato — this was hands down one of the best shows. Oh and the VOCALS?&#8221;

Lovato&#8217;s next show will take place on April 16 in Washington, D.C., after which the singer will stop through Philadelphia, Toronto, Boston, New York, Detroit, Chicago, San Francisco, Seattle, Dallas and several other North American cities. The tour will conclude in May with a trio of shows in Lovato&#8217;s home state of Texas.

There&#8217;s no telling how the setlist may change from show to show, but below, check out all the songs &#8212; and which of Lovato&#8217;s albums they belong to &#8212; from the It&#8217;s Not That Deep Tour kickoff.
